{"parentUuid":"4fb55078-be06-419d-bd20-4f003bfb9ea1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"44593253-6ae0-4c5c-bede-0f4720f09c7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PN6T8ExDtkgJTq47kiZDkU","type":"tool_result","content":"setValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nvalueForKeyFakeAssocArray:28: command not found: _decode\nvalueForKeyFakeAssocArray:28: command not found: _decode\n=== remote branch commit via gh API (no git transfer) ===\nMerge branch 'main' into feat/bigquery-auto-create-table\n=== files changed on remote branch vs main (gh compare) ===\nfeat(sink-bigquery): auto-create the target table and dataset on first sync\n\nThe BigQuery sink now creates the destination table (and dataset) when it is\nmissing — or re-creates it when it exists **without a schema** (e.g. one made\nby a bare `bq mk`) — inferring the schema from the first written page. A\nfirst-ever sync can never assume the table already exists. Previously an\n`overwrite` run failed at `begin_overwrite` (`CREATE … LIKE` requires a\nschema'd target: 404 when missing, \"does not have a schema\" when schemaless)\nand the append/insertAll path never auto-created.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6c149d99-1a5e-42c5-8d42-b88eefe35e23","timestamp":"2026-08-24T05:18:38.576Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"setValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nsetValueForKeyFakeAssocArray:27: command not found: _encode\nvalueForKeyFakeAssocArray:28: command not found: _decode\nvalueForKeyFakeAssocArray:28: command not found: _decode\n=== remote branch commit via gh API (no git transfer) ===\nMerge branch 'main' into feat/bigquery-auto-create-table\n=== files changed on remote branch vs main (gh compare) ===\nfeat(sink-bigquery): auto-create the target table and dataset on first sync\n\nThe BigQuery sink now creates the destination table (and dataset) when it is\nmissing — or re-creates it when it exists **without a schema** (e.g. one made\nby a bare `bq mk`) — inferring the schema from the first written page. A\nfirst-ever sync can never assume the table already exists. Previously an\n`overwrite` run failed at `begin_overwrite` (`CREATE … LIKE` requires a\nschema'd target: 404 when missing, \"does not have a schema\" when schemaless)\nand the append/insertAll path never auto-created.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4fb55078-be06-419d-bd20-4f003bfb9ea1","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.228","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
