{"parentUuid":"896db589-194b-47e5-8e21-33ea0dd6488d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeM5SbjSWQawdUM9bM1Xj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D2JMWEKxBDMFCLJ865VBv4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nF=\"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/reference_pre_push_gate_checklist.md\"\nif [ -f \"$F\" ]; then\ncat >> \"$F\" <<'EOF'\n\n## CI failed on already-\"fixed\" lints (2026-08): commit + re-run the FULL gate after fixing\nBit hard on PR #577: after the first `--workspace --all-targets --all-features` clippy failed (missing struct field + collapsible_if + redundant_guards in faucet-cli), I edited the fixes, re-ran clippy **-p faucet-cli only** (green), then moved on — and **never committed those edits**, so the pushed commit lacked them → CI Clippy (exit 101) AND Test (cli lib test wouldn't compile) both failed. Two rules: (1) after fixing a gate, re-run the SAME broad command (`--workspace --all-targets --all-features`), not a narrowed `-p`; (2) before pushing, `git status` must be clean of the intended edits — a local green run means nothing if the fix isn't in the commit. Also: the PR branch may get \"Update branch\" (merge main) between pushes → fetch + `git rebase --onto <remote-head> <old-base>` your fix commit rather than force-dropping main's commits.\nEOF\necho \"memory updated\"\nfi","description":"Record CI-fix lesson in memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":869,"cache_read_input_tokens":782542,"output_tokens":972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":869,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},