{"parentUuid":"1e03452b-2b63-4ae9-8d52-5fa188e84d56","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- datadog-s3-logs-agent: Read Drivetrain production Datadog logs archived in S3 (s3://dt-logs-archive/datadog/logs/) by assuming the cross-account `prod-ui-read-access` role in prod account 865992467666. Trigger for any request that needs historical logs beyond Datadog's hot/indexed retention, or when Datadog's `online_archives_and_indexes` returns no hits but you need raw logs. Examples: 'find when user X was created', 'pull the trace for request-id Y', 'did this tenant emit log Z last month', 'grep production drive logs for pattern P from Jan 2026'. Use this instead of the Datadog MCP when the time range is old (older than ~30d), when the query returns 0 hits from hot/archive indexes, or when the user explicitly wants the S3 archive.\n- datasets-manage-schema-agent: Understand and work with Drivetrain's three-layer dataset architecture (src_ → usr_ → out_) and the Manage Schema feature. Use this skill when working on dataset pipeline code, manage schema UI, DatasetColumnService, DbtService model generation, DTX builds, debugging dataset type/schema issues, or understanding how raw source data becomes user-facing tables. Trigger phrases include \"manage schema\", \"dataset columns\", \"src_ usr_ out_\", \"DatasetColumn\", \"DatasetColumnService\", \"DatasetColumnApi\", \"dataset architecture\", \"dataset pipeline\", \"source schema\", \"primary schema\", \"usr_ model\", \"out_ model\", \"column selection\", \"column rename\", \"column type change\", \"type cast\", \"STRING to DATE\", \"dataset_columns table\", \"DTX build\", \"buildDtxUserSelectionModelContents\", \"user selection model\", \"transform model\", \"manage schema modal\", \"column alert\", \"COLUMN_MISSING\", \"dataset type\", \"DatasetType\".\n- drive-backend-agent: Make Java backend code changes in DrivetrainAi/drive and open a PR. Use this skill for any drive backend work — adding a new connector, connector credential/config validations, dataset transformations (TransformService), connector data refresh / sync scheduling, new API endpoints, repository/service/DB-model changes. Trigger phrases include \"add a connector to drive\", \"modify DtxService\", \"add validation for connector credentials\", \"fix TransformService\", \"change sync scheduling\", \"new drive API endpoint\", \"drive backend ENG-XXXXX\", \"add support for a new source in drive\". Base branch is main-v3. Java tests require JDK 11. Does NOT cover drive-frontend (use drive-frontend-agent) or Temporal workflow/worker state-machine logic (use temporal-workflow-agent).\n- drive-frontend-agent: Make React/TypeScript changes in DrivetrainAi/drive-frontend and open a PR. Use this skill for any drive UI work — dataset grid behavior, manage-schema modal, column ordering/visibility, error messages and field display, sync-scheduling UI, plan/board tables, role/folder gating, connector setup screens, and frontend API-call fixes. Trigger phrases include \"fix the manage schema modal\", \"column ordering wrong in the grid\", \"error message in drive UI\", \"update the sync schedule UI\", \"drive-frontend ENG-XXXXX\", \"wire up a connector in the dataset UI\", \"frontend bug in drive\". This is the single largest source of Spartans tickets. Does NOT cover Java backend (use drive-backend-agent).\n- drive-mcp-oauth-agent: Understand and debug the MCP OAuth 2.0 and Atlas token flows in the DrivetrainAi/drive repo — the auth that lets AI clients (Claude, ChatGPT, internal MCP tooling) and the Atlas backend call Drive on behalf of a user. Use this skill when investigating /oauth2/authorize or /oauth2/token failures, /.well-known/* discovery misbehavior (Okta fallback when an SSO tenant is expected), Atlas 'atlas-' prefixed token issues, MCP clients getting 401 or token-expired errors, token-lifetime bugs (tokens expiring in seconds or lasting decades), McpAuthFilter behavior, or anything touching McpOAuthService, AtlasService, OAuthDiscoveryApi, OAuthBearerAuthenticationProvider, or JwtService. Trigger phrases: 'MCP auth failing', 'Claude MCP 401', 'OAuth token expired immediately', 'atlas token invalid', 'discovery returning Okta for an SSO tenant', '/oauth2/token failing', 'SP-initiated MCP', 'ENG-578 ENG-74054 ENG-74371 ENG-74519'.\n- drive-saml-sso-agent: Understand and debug SAML SSO browser-login flow in the DrivetrainAi/drive repo. Use this skill when investigating user login issues via SSO (Okta/IdP), SAMLResponse parsing errors, tenant resolution failures on id.drivetrain.ai, SP-initiated vs IdP-initiated flows, frequent logout reports, cross-tenant JIT provisioning bugs, or anything touching `SamlApi`, `SessionRequestInterceptor`, `TenantFilter`, or `/api/v1/public/login-by-username`. Trigger phrases: 'SAML error', 'SSO login failing', 'user can't log in via SSO', 'SAMLResponse invalid', 'tenant -1 / id.drivetrain.ai', 'SP-initiated SSO', 'IdP-initiated SSO', 'login-by-username', 'frequent logout SSO', 'cross-tenant leak', 'JIT provisioning wrong tenant', 'base64 SAMLResponse', 'auth tenant', 'ENG-74019 ENG-74152 ENG-73982 ENG-74284 ENG-74519'. Contains the architecture, endpoint map, and the exact failure modes we've hit (and fixed) in recent months — consult this before guessing at SAML code.\n- drive-tools-page-agent: Use when an LLM (or human via Claude) needs to pick or run a \"Drivetrainer Tools page\" admin operation in `DrivetrainAi/drive` (`main-v3`) — i.e. anything exposed at `GET /api/v1/system/tools` and rendered as the gated tools page for Drivetrain employees. Trigger phrases include \"tools page\", \"Drivetrainer tools\", \"system/tools\", \"SystemService.buildApiResponse\", \"ToolsApiResponse\", \"trigger DTX\", \"trigger DBT\", \"sync-dbt\", \"sync-dtx\", \"system/data/trigger-transforms\", \"Soft Delete Connector Instance\", \"Mark All Syncing Connector Instances As Connected\", \"Configure Fiscal Month and Year\", \"Reset User Password to Temporary Password\", \"Clear Drive Cache\", \"Temporal terminate workflow\", \"Atlas upload embeddings\", \"Sandbox refresh\", \"tenant onboarding fix tool\", \"which tool should I run\", \"is this tool destructive\", \"tools page idempotent\".\n- e2e-testing-agent: End-to-end testing skill for Drivetrain backend features. Use when you need to: test changes via APIs, create dummy data in BigQuery and PostgreSQL, trigger DTX builds, verify generated SQL in dtx repos, check health records, clone/inspect dtx and dbt repos, or run automated test suites against localhost. This skill covers the full testing loop: setup dummy data → hit APIs → wait for Temporal → verify dtx output → check health records.\n- ecs-task-failure-analyzer: Pinpoint the root cause of a failed ECS task by fetching its CloudWatch logs from the task ARN/ID and analyzing the error. Use this skill whenever the user shares an ECS task ARN, task ID, or asks \"why did this task fail\" / \"read the logs for task X\" / \"what failed in this task ARN\" — especially for iPaaS connectors (non-meltano) and Meltano taps. Trigger phrases include \"task arn\", \"task failed\", \"ecs task\", \"fetch logs for task\", \"why did task X fail\", \"pinpoint failure\", \"read task logs\", \"b94f94...\" (raw 32-char ECS task IDs), \"airflow worker task failed\", \"ipaas task failed\", \"meltano task failed\", \"fetch failure\". Always use this skill when given an ECS task ID/ARN to investigate.\n- error-messages: Transform raw Drivetrain pipeline errors (fetch / dbt / dtx) into structured user-facing messages — title, message, resolution, internal_resolution, severity, customer_actionable. Use this skill whenever you need to interpret or rewrite a raw error from Drivetrain's data pipeline (Airflow/Temporal failures, ECS task stop reasons, dbt test failures, dbt build errors, DTX schema/expectations failures, connector-specific tap errors). Trigger phrases include \"humanize this error\", \"rewrite this train error\", \"what does this error mean for the user\", \"transform raw error into UI message\", \"DBT failure for tenant X\", \"DTX failure\", \"tap-X error\", \"fetch failure for a connector\", or any time you see raw error strings from a Drivetrain sync that need to be turned into structured customer-facing output.\n- graphify: any input (code, docs, papers, images) - knowledge graph - clustered communities - HTML + JSON + audit report\n- ipaas-connector-development-agent: Build and register new iPaaS connectors in the DrivetrainAi/ipaas repo. Use this skill when the user wants to add a new data source connector, create a new connector script, register a connector in Airflow, or scaffold iPaaS connector boilerplate. Trigger phrases include \"add a new connector to ipaas\", \"build an ipaas connector for X\", \"scaffold a new ipaas script\", \"register connector in airflow_utils\", \"create ipaas integration for X\", \"new data source for ipaas\", \"add X to ipaas\". Always use this skill for iPaaS connector development work. Do NOT use to DEBUG a failing connector (use ipaas-connector-troubleshooting-agent); Singer-tap connectors are a different path (use meltano-tap-development-agent).\n- ipaas-connector-troubleshooting-agent: Debug and FIX failing iPaaS connectors in the DrivetrainAi/ipaas repo, and open a fix PR. Use this skill when the user reports a connector is failing, a tenant's sync is broken, data isn't loading to BigQuery, an ECS task is erroring, or they need to investigate iPaaS connector issues. Trigger phrases include \"ipaas connector failing\", \"sync failing for tenant X\", \"connector not loading data\", \"ECS task failing\", \"ipaas error\", \"connector broken\", \"data not syncing\", \"fix ipaas connector\", \"debug ipaas\", \"connector throwing error\", \"BigQuery load failing\". Categorizes failures (auth, HTTP, schema, pagination, BigQuery-load) and applies a minimal fix. Negative triggers — to BUILD a new connector use ipaas-connector-development-agent; if it is a Singer tap (tap-CONNECTOR) use meltano-tap-connectors-agent, not this skill. Category — Workflow Automation.\n- meltano-tap-connectors-agent: Connector-specific reference and debugging guide for all DrivetrainAi Meltano Singer taps (tap-CONNECTOR). Use this skill when debugging a specific connector tap, investigating why a stream is empty, fixing auth issues, understanding what streams/config fields a tap supports, or checking known quirks for a connector. Trigger phrases include \"tap-hubspot isn't syncing\", \"why is tap-netsuite slow\", \"what streams does tap-xero have\", \"tap-intacct failing with XML error\", \"debug tap-stripe\", \"config fields for tap-bamboohr\", \"tap-quickbooks pagination issue\", \"what does tap-zohobooks need\", and any question about a specific tap's behavior, config, or streams.\n- meltano-tap-development-agent: Meltano Tap Development Skill\n- onboarding-ask-agent: Investigate and fix tenant onboarding failures tagged with the 'onboarding-ask' label in Linear. Trigger this skill whenever the user mentions an onboarding-ask issue, provides a Linear ENG ticket with tenant onboarding failures, asks you to investigate why a new tenant's data isn't loading, mentions DTX/dbt/HRIS failures for a specific tenant, or says 'investigate onboarding issue for tenant X'. Always use this skill when you see patterns like 'onboarding-ask', 'tenant N failing', 'new tenant setup failing', 'dbt error for tenant', 'dtx failure for tenant'. The skill investigates root cause via Datadog logs, GitHub repos (dbt and dtx tenant repos, drive, std dbt repos), and delegates the fix to the matching repo skill (which opens the PR). Do NOT use for routine dbt/model changes that are not a pipeline failure (use tenant-dbt-repo-agent), or for debugging a shipped connector tap (use meltano-tap-connectors-agent).\n- spartans-linear-report-agent: Report Linear issue activity for the Spartans group of Engineering-team assignees (e.g. Sateesh, Lomash, Irfan, Harsh, Pawan, Manav, Zainab, Kartikey — full roster in skills/_shared/spartans-roster.md). Trigger this skill for any request about 'Spartans' Linear activity: issues closed, completed, in review, day-wise counts, weekly reports, or per-person breakdowns. Examples: 'linears closed by spartans this week', 'spartans day-wise count', 'how many tickets did spartans complete', 'spartans report for last week'. Note: 'Spartans' is NOT a Linear team/label/project — it is a fixed list of assignees. Category — MCP Enhancement.\n- spartans-onboarding: Navigation layer for new Spartans engineers. Use this skill to understand what a Drivetrain internal system does, find where code or docs live, know which skill to invoke for a task, or understand how the data platform works end-to-end. Does not execute tasks — routes to the correct skill for actual work.\n- spartans-pr-router: Orchestrator for resolving a Spartans Linear ticket end-to-end into a merged PR. Reads the ENG ticket, classifies which repo + layer the change belongs to, and routes to the correct repo-specific skill (drive-backend-agent, drive-frontend-agent, temporal-workflow-agent, xiphos-agent, torque-agent, standard-dbt-repo-agent, tenant-dbt-repo-agent, meltano-tap-development-agent, ipaas-connector-development-agent, onboarding-ask-agent). It opens no PRs itself — specialists do. Use whenever the user hands you a Linear issue to implement. Trigger phrases: \"resolve ENG-XXXXX\", \"implement this Linear\", \"open a PR for ENG-XXXXX\", \"handle this Spartans ticket\", \"make the code change for ENG-XXXXX\", \"fix this ticket\", \"pick up ENG-XXXXX\", \"what repo does this ENG belong to\". Always use this skill first when the work originates from a Linear ticket and you don't already know the exact repo. Category — Workflow Automation.\n- standard-dbt-repo-agent: Clone and modify a STANDARD (baseline) dbt connector repo named dbt_CONNECTOR (e.g. dbt_hubspot, dbt_netsuite, dbt_quickbooks) in the DrivetrainAi org, and open a PR. These repos define the canonical models, macros, and tests shared across ALL tenants for a connector. Use this skill to add/edit standard models, fix a connector's baseline transformation, add/modify macros, update schema.yml, or add multi-instance/union logic. Trigger phrases include \"fix dbt_hubspot model\", \"update the standard netsuite model\", \"add macro to dbt_xero\", \"multi-instance support in a standard dbt repo\", \"standard dbt connector repo\", \"baseline model for a connector\". DISTINCT from tenant-dbt-repo-agent, which handles TENANT repos named dbt-NNN (e.g. dbt-488). If the ask names a numeric tenant repo, use tenant-dbt-repo-agent instead.\n- temporal-workflow-agent: Make changes to Temporal workflow and worker logic and open a PR. IMPORTANT — Drivetrain's Temporal workflows/activities live INSIDE the DrivetrainAi/drive Java repo (flow/workflows, flow/activities), not a separate repo. Use this skill when the change is about workflow state-machine behavior — re-enqueue/re-run logic, signals, child workflows, retry/timeout policies, activity orchestration, workflow versioning, or fixing a stuck/looping workflow. Trigger phrases include \"fix the transform workflow\", \"stop the DTX re-enqueue loop\", \"workflow keeps retrying\", \"add a signal to a workflow\", \"change activity orchestration\", \"temporal workflow ENG-XXXXX\", \"worker not picking up tasks\". For plain service/DB/API drive backend changes use drive-backend-agent; for sync health-record writes use drive-backend-agent (data-refresh layer).\n- tenant-dbt-repo-agent: Clone and make changes to tenant-specific dbt repos (named dbt-TENANT_ID, e.g. dbt-488) in the DrivetrainAi GitHub org. Use this skill whenever the user asks to modify a tenant's dbt repo, add/edit/delete dbt models, sources, macros, tests, seeds, or packages for a specific tenant. Trigger phrases include \"update dbt for tenant X\", \"add a model to dbt-123\", \"clone dbt repo for tenant\", \"make dbt changes for X\", \"custom dbt transformation for tenant\", \"fix dbt model for X\", \"add source for connector Y in tenant X\". Also trigger when the user references a dbt-NUMBER repo, mentions custom dbt work, or asks about tenant-specific transformations. Always use this skill even if the user just says \"dbt changes\" or mentions a tenant ID in the context of transformations. Do NOT use for standard baseline dbt_CONNECTOR repos (use standard-dbt-repo-agent instead).\n- torque-agent: Make changes to the DrivetrainAi/torque repo (Python/FastAPI dbt-job runner) and open a PR. Use this skill for torque work — the dbt job lifecycle, job state/heartbeat in S3, the async task router, build-slot/resource lifecycle, and torque settings/deployment config. Trigger phrases include \"fix torque job heartbeat\", \"torque dbt job stuck\", \"build slot lifecycle in torque\", \"torque router task\", \"memory cleanup in torque workdir\", \"torque ENG-XXXXX\", \"dbt run orchestration in torque\". Base branch is staging (per Drivetrain convention) — but recent PRs were observed on preprod; confirm the base at PR time. Does NOT cover the dbt models themselves (use tenant-dbt-repo-agent / standard-dbt-repo-agent).\n- transformations-agent: Reference guide for understanding, debugging, and correcting Drivetrain transformation rules — the system that writes ui_transform steps to the dtx tenant repo's dbt_project.yml. Use this skill when: investigating _dt_ prefix errors, debugging mark_as_dim / lookup / add steps, reading transform_rules in dbt_project.yml, understanding how transformations are persisted to DTX repos, or working with de-lorean to parse/upload transformation steps. Always read this skill before acting on any DTX issue in the onboarding-ask-agent.\n- ui-transforms-agent: Understand and work with Drivetrain's UI Transforms feature and dataset architecture (src_ → usr_ → out_ pipeline). Covers the spreadsheet-like transform builder (add columns, filter, join, rename, unpivot, financial transforms), the Manage Schema layer (column selection, renaming, type casting from source to user tables), and the three-layer dataset model. Use this skill when working on transform-related code in backend-drive or drive-frontend, debugging transform save/preview issues, understanding how datasets flow from source to output, working on manage schema, or adding new transform types. Trigger phrases include \"UI transforms\", \"dataset transforms\", \"manage schema\", \"dataset columns\", \"src_ usr_ out_\", \"DatasetColumnService\", \"TransformService\", \"TransformationApi\", \"ui_transform_macro\", \"add column transform\", \"transform preview not working\", \"how do transforms get saved to dbt\", \"column rename\", \"column type change\".\n- xiphos-agent: Make changes to the DrivetrainAi/xiphos repo (Python/FastAPI connector service) and open a PR. Use this skill for xiphos work — adding or modifying a meltano connector service, ECS environment variables passed to a connector run, pagination/auth/config behavior for a connector, or the connector v2 service layer. Trigger phrases include \"add env var to a connector in xiphos\", \"fix connector pagination in xiphos\", \"xiphos connector service for X\", \"modify ecs_env_variables\", \"xiphos ENG-XXXXX\", \"connector run config in xiphos\". Base branch is main. Does NOT cover the drive connector enum (use drive-backend-agent) or the Singer tap itself (use meltano-tap-development-agent).\n- my-usage: Check my Bedrock Claude Code budget usage.\n- agent-spartan:trains-investigation: Default root-cause analysis of current train failures — pulls Datadog + ECS logs, classifies transient vs real, reports RCA.\n- agent-spartan:trains: Snapshot of current Drivetrain train (pipeline) failures across tenants — fetch / dbt / dtx / recon.\n- agent-spartan:datadog-s3-logs-agent: Read Drivetrain production Datadog logs archived in S3 (s3://dt-logs-archive/datadog/logs/) by assuming the cross-account `prod-ui-read-access` role in prod account 865992467666. Trigger for any request that needs historical logs beyond Datadog's hot/indexed retention, or when Datadog's `online_archives_and_indexes` returns no hits but you need raw logs. Examples: 'find when user X was created', 'pull the trace for request-id Y', 'did this tenant emit log Z last month', 'grep production drive logs for pattern P from Jan 2026'. Use this instead of the Datadog MCP when the time range is old (older than ~30d), when the query returns 0 hits from hot/archive indexes, or when the user explicitly wants the S3 archive.\n- agent-spartan:datasets-manage-schema-agent: Understand and work with Drivetrain's three-layer dataset architecture (src_ → usr_ → out_) and the Manage Schema feature. Use this skill when working on dataset pipeline code, manage schema UI, DatasetColumnService, DbtService model generation, DTX builds, debugging dataset type/schema issues, or understanding how raw source data becomes user-facing tables. Trigger phrases include \"manage schema\", \"dataset columns\", \"src_ usr_ out_\", \"DatasetColumn\", \"DatasetColumnService\", \"DatasetColumnApi\", \"dataset architecture\", \"dataset pipeline\", \"source schema\", \"primary schema\", \"usr_ model\", \"out_ model\", \"column selection\", \"column rename\", \"column type change\", \"type cast\", \"STRING to DATE\", \"dataset_columns table\", \"DTX build\", \"buildDtxUserSelectionModelContents\", \"user selection model\", \"transform model\", \"manage schema modal\", \"column alert\", \"COLUMN_MISSING\", \"dataset type\", \"DatasetType\".\n- agent-spartan:drive-backend-agent: Make Java backend code changes in DrivetrainAi/drive and open a PR. Use this skill for any drive backend work — adding a new connector, connector credential/config validations, dataset transformations (TransformService), connector data refresh / sync scheduling, new API endpoints, repository/service/DB-model changes. Trigger phrases include \"add a connector to drive\", \"modify DtxService\", \"add validation for connector credentials\", \"fix TransformService\", \"change sync scheduling\", \"new drive API endpoint\", \"drive backend ENG-XXXXX\", \"add support for a new source in drive\". Base branch is main-v3. Java tests require JDK 11. Does NOT cover drive-frontend (use drive-frontend-agent) or Temporal workflow/worker state-machine logic (use temporal-workflow-agent).\n- agent-spartan:drive-frontend-agent\n- agent-spartan:drive-mcp-oauth-agent\n- agent-spartan:drive-saml-sso-agent\n- agent-spartan:drive-tools-page-agent\n- agent-spartan:e2e-testing-agent: End-to-end testing skill for Drivetrain backend features. Use when you need to: test changes via APIs, create dummy data in BigQuery and PostgreSQL, trigger DTX builds, verify generated SQL in dtx repos, check health records, clone/inspect dtx and dbt repos, or run automated test suites against localhost. This skill covers the full testing loop: setup dummy data → hit APIs → wait for Temporal → verify dtx output → check health records.\n- agent-spartan:ecs-task-failure-analyzer\n- agent-spartan:error-messages\n- agent-spartan:ipaas-connector-development-agent\n- agent-spartan:ipaas-connector-troubleshooting-agent\n- agent-spartan:meltano-tap-connectors-agent\n- agent-spartan:onboarding-ask-agent\n- agent-spartan:spartans-linear-report-agent\n- agent-spartan:spartans-onboarding\n- agent-spartan:spartans-pr-router\n- agent-spartan:standard-dbt-repo-agent\n- agent-spartan:temporal-workflow-agent\n- agent-spartan:tenant-dbt-repo-agent\n- agent-spartan:torque-agent\n- agent-spartan:trains-transform-rerun-agent\n- agent-spartan:transformations-agent\n- agent-spartan:ui-transforms-agent\n- agent-spartan:xiphos-agent\n- frontend-design:frontend-design: Guidance for distinctive, intentional visual design when building new UI or reshaping an existing one. Helps with aesthetic direction, typography, and making choices that don't read as templated defaults.\n- dataviz: Use this skill whenever you are about to create ANY chart, graph, plot, dashboard, or data visualization, in ANY output medium — an HTML or React artifact, inline SVG, plotting code in any library (matplotlib, plotly, d3, Recharts, …), an image/PNG you will render and upload, or a chart shared into Slack. Read it BEFORE writing the first line of chart code, choosing chart colors, building a stat tile / meter / KPI row, or laying out a dashboard. Produces visualizations that read as one system — elegant, accessible, consistent in light and dark — using a brand-neutral placeholder palette you swap for your own. Teaches a design-system-agnostic method: a form heuristic, a color formula with a runnable validator, mark specs, and interaction rules. A validated default palette is documented in `references/palette.md` — swap that file's values for your brand's. Triggers on: \"chart\", \"graph\", \"plot\", \"data viz\", \"visualization\", \"dashboard\", \"analytics\", \"visualize data\", \"categorical colors\", \"sequential / diverging palette\", \"stat tile\", \"sparkline\", \"heatmap\", \"legend\", \"axis\", \"tooltip\", \"chart colors\", \"color by series\".\n- artifact-design: Design guidance and fundamentals for Artifacts.\n- artifact-diagramming: Diagramming know-how for Artifacts — when a picture earns its place, how to draw one that shows the real mechanism, and the inline-SVG mechanics that keep it legible in both themes.\n- artifact-capabilities: Runtime capabilities a published Artifact page can be granted — behavior static HTML cannot provide on its own, such as the page reading live or connected data, keeping state shared across viewers, handing the viewer a file to save, or updating and republishing itself. Serves this user's live capability roster and the typed call definitions. Load it whenever the user asks for an artifact needing any such runtime behavior.\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- code-review: Review the current diff, or a PR number/branch/path target, for correctness bugs and reuse/simplification/efficiency cleanups at the given effort level (low/medium: fewer, high-confidence findings; high→max: broader coverage, may include uncertain findings); with no level given, it reuses the level you typed last. Pass --comment to post findings as inline PR comments, or --fix to apply the findings to the working tree after the review.\n- simplify: Review the changed code for reuse, simplification, efficiency, and altitude cleanups, then apply the fixes. Quality only — it does not hunt for bugs; use /code-review for that.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace. - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- schedule: Create, update, list, or run scheduled cloud agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule. - When the user wants to schedule a recurring cloud agent, set up automated tasks, create a cron job for Claude Code, or manage their scheduled agents/routines. Also use when the user wants a one-time scheduled run (\"run this once at 3pm\", \"remind me to check X tomorrow\").\n- claude-api: Reference for the Claude API / Anthropic SDK — model ids, pricing, params, streaming, tool use, MCP, agents, caching, token counting, model migration.\nTRIGGER — read BEFORE opening the target file; don't skip because it \"looks like a one-liner\" — whenever: the prompt names Claude/Anthropic in any form (Claude, Anthropic, Fable, Opus, Sonnet, Haiku, `anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai`, `claude-*`, `us.anthropic.*`, `[1m]`); the user asks about an LLM (pricing/model choice/limits/caching) — never answer from memory; OR the task is LLM-shaped with provider unstated (agent/MCP/tool-definition/multi-agent/RAG/LLM-judge/computer-use; generate/summarize/extract/classify/rewrite/converse over NL; debugging refusals/cutoffs/streaming/tool-calls/tokens).\nSKIP only when another provider is being worked on (overrides all triggers): OpenAI/GPT/Gemini/Llama/Mistral/Cohere/Ollama named in the query; OR `grep -rE 'openai|langchain_openai|google.generativeai|genai|mistralai|cohere|ollama'` over the project hits (run this grep FIRST if no provider named — don't Read the file).\n- claude-in-chrome: Automates your Chrome browser to interact with web pages - clicking elements, filling forms, capturing screenshots, reading console logs, and navigating sites. Opens pages in new tabs within your existing Chrome session. Requires site-level permissions before executing (configured in the extension). - When the user wants to interact with web pages, automate browser tasks, capture screenshots, read console logs, or perform any browser-based actions. Always invoke BEFORE attempting to use any mcp__claude-in-chrome__* tools.\n- run: Launch and drive this project's app to see a change working. Use when asked to run, start, or screenshot the app, or to confirm a change works in the real app (not just tests). First looks for a project skill that already covers launching the app; otherwise falls back to built-in patterns per project type (CLI, server, TUI, Electron, browser-driven, library).\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","skillCount":71,"isInitial":true,"names":["datadog-s3-logs-agent","datasets-manage-schema-agent","drive-backend-agent","drive-frontend-agent","drive-mcp-oauth-agent","drive-saml-sso-agent","drive-tools-page-agent","e2e-testing-agent","ecs-task-failure-analyzer","error-messages","graphify","ipaas-connector-development-agent","ipaas-connector-troubleshooting-agent","meltano-tap-connectors-agent","meltano-tap-development-agent","onboarding-ask-agent","spartans-linear-report-agent","spartans-onboarding","spartans-pr-router","standard-dbt-repo-agent","temporal-workflow-agent","tenant-dbt-repo-agent","torque-agent","transformations-agent","ui-transforms-agent","xiphos-agent","my-usage","agent-spartan:trains-investigation","agent-spartan:trains","agent-spartan:datadog-s3-logs-agent","agent-spartan:datasets-manage-schema-agent","agent-spartan:drive-backend-agent","agent-spartan:drive-frontend-agent","agent-spartan:drive-mcp-oauth-agent","agent-spartan:drive-saml-sso-agent","agent-spartan:drive-tools-page-agent","agent-spartan:e2e-testing-agent","agent-spartan:ecs-task-failure-analyzer","agent-spartan:error-messages","agent-spartan:ipaas-connector-development-agent","agent-spartan:ipaas-connector-troubleshooting-agent","agent-spartan:meltano-tap-connectors-agent","agent-spartan:onboarding-ask-agent","agent-spartan:spartans-linear-report-agent","agent-spartan:spartans-onboarding","agent-spartan:spartans-pr-router","agent-spartan:standard-dbt-repo-agent","agent-spartan:temporal-workflow-agent","agent-spartan:tenant-dbt-repo-agent","agent-spartan:torque-agent","agent-spartan:trains-transform-rerun-agent","agent-spartan:transformations-agent","agent-spartan:ui-transforms-agent","agent-spartan:xiphos-agent","frontend-design:frontend-design","dataviz","artifact-design","artifact-diagramming","artifact-capabilities","update-config","keybindings-help","code-review","simplify","fewer-permission-prompts","loop","schedule","claude-api","claude-in-chrome","run","init","security-review"]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a6a2082f-fa53-40a5-a4ce-76cfc5454f59","timestamp":"2026-08-24T08:49:21.679Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/bigquery-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
