{"parentUuid":"ef4e577f-8627-48a8-8e30-c15652d1bede","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeMJfSUwvKafrAamNfYxf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Auto-merge is armed and the coverage commit (`c2c3260e`) is pushed. CI is re-running.\n\n## Status\n- **Root cause of the last red:** only the 90% patch-coverage floor (89.12%) — all tests passed.\n- **Fix:** added ~35–38 lines of targeted coverage (params `${map:}`/computed error branches, REST captured-substitution, BigQuery error paths, `RequestAuth::with_captured`, expand reserved-token-in-transform), taking patch coverage from 89.12% → an estimated **~94%** (comfortably over the 90% gate, near your 95% target).\n- **Gate discipline held this time:** full `fmt --check` + `--workspace --all-targets --all-features` clippy, both green on the exact committed tree, *before* pushing.\n\nCI will now run Coverage on `c2c3260e`; if it lands ≥90% (it should), auto-merge merges #577. I can't measure the exact patch % locally (the `--all-features` instrumented build doesn't link on this arm64 box), so CI is the source of truth — if it reports, say, 94% and you want the full 95%, tell me and I'll cover a few more of the remaining lines.\n\nBackground watchers get culled here, so I'll check the result on the next exchange (or ping me). Once #577 merges I'll start **#580**."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_read_input_tokens":872299,"output_tokens":447,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":447,"cache_read_input_tokens":872299,"cache_creation_input_tokens":672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"