{"parentUuid":"dd939bc6-1830-4d09-aef5-2bba16adc83f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ad4dec01-0e45-4755-83ce-1d6f9d7f8809","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012NS4VQUsXFMParxNk9aKXv","type":"tool_result","content":"=== replicate clone exists? ===\n-rw-r--r--  1 c-sikawats  staff  85452  1 Aug 07:11 /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/replicate/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md\n=== is the replicate CLAUDE.md a symlink already? ===\n(regular file, not a symlink)\n\n=== sizes / line counts ===\n     213 /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md\n     596 /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/replicate/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md\n     809 total\n\n=== diff (replicate vs current) — lines only in replicate (<) could be valuable ===\n3c3\n< ## Library Purpose\n---\n> `faucet-stream` is a modular, config-driven Rust data-pipeline toolkit: pluggable **source** and **sink** connectors plus a `faucet` CLI binary that runs pipelines declaratively from YAML/JSON (no Rust code required). Cargo workspace, 92 crates (91 libraries + the `faucet-cli` binary); all connector crates depend only on `faucet-core`, and the umbrella `faucet-stream` + the CLI pull in every connector via optional features. `faucet serve` (opt-in) adds a long-running HTTP control-plane runtime alongside one-shot `run` and the `schedule` cron runtime.\n5c5\n< `faucet-stream` is a modular, config-driven data pipeline toolkit for Rust with pluggable **source** and **sink** connectors, plus a `faucet` CLI binary that runs pipelines declaratively from YAML/JSON — no Rust code required.\n---\n> This file holds the **always-on rules**. Situational detail lives in on-demand reference files under `.claude/rules/` (see below) — read the relevant one when its trigger applies.\n7,9c7\n< - **Sources** fetch data from external systems (e.g. REST APIs).\n< - **Sinks** write data to external systems (e.g. BigQuery).\n< - **`faucet` CLI** (`cli/`) wires source → transforms → sink together based on a config file.\n---\n> ## Reference files (`.claude/rules/`, read on demand)\n11c9\n< Design goal: callers configure a source or sink once, call `fetch_all()` or `write_batch()`, and get/write all records — no manual pagination loop, no auth boilerplate. Rust users embed the library directly; everyone else runs the `faucet` binary.\n---\n> These are **not** auto-loaded. `Read` the matching file when the situation applies:\n13c11,16\n< This workspace produces both library crates (`faucet-core` + every connector and state backend) and the `faucet` CLI binary. There is no database, no migrations, and no server.\n---\n> | File | Read when… |\n> |---|---|\n> | `.claude/rules/architecture.md` | you need to know which crate/module holds something, a trait's exact contract, a subsystem's internals (faucet-core modules, connector conventions, CLI, scheduling, serve, observability, lineage), or the feature-flag layout + the full crate table. |\n> | `.claude/rules/connectors.md` | adding/modifying any source/sink, or touching performance/streaming/batching, DLQ, **exactly-once delivery**, **write modes / upsert**, quality checks, secrets interpolation, REST pagination, compression, config loading/schema, or error handling. |\n> | `.claude/rules/publishing.md` | releasing crates to crates.io (release-plz or the manual fallback), or touching docs.rs build setup / the mdBook docs site. |\n> | `.claude/rules/maintenance.md` | a post-merge cleanup request, or after changing a connector / config field / CLI command / public API (the trigger→update table for keeping docs, examples, the capability matrix, and counts in sync). |\n15c18\n< ## Workspace Structure\n---\n> ## Primary Goal\n17c20\n< Cargo workspace, 91 crates (90 libraries + the `faucet-cli` binary). All connector crates depend only on `faucet-core`; the umbrella `faucet-stream` and the `faucet-cli` binary depend on every connector + state crate via optional features.\n---\n> **All sources and sinks must be as fast, efficient, and reliable as possible.** This is the number one priority for every decision — architecture, implementation, dependency choice, and API design. Performance and reliability are not afterthoughts; they are the reason this library exists. Every connector should be the fastest way to move data between its endpoints in Rust. The concrete performance checklist + streaming/DLQ/exactly-once/quality/secrets internals live in `.claude/rules/connectors.md`.\n19,111c22\n< | Crate | Path | Description |\n< |-------|------|-------------|\n< | `faucet-core` | `crates/core/` | Shared types, traits (`Source`, `Sink`, `AuthProvider`), pipeline orchestration, transforms, error types |\n< | `faucet-auth` | `crates/auth/` | Shared single-flight auth providers (`StaticProvider`, OAuth2 client-credentials / refresh-with-rotation, token-endpoint) implementing `faucet_core::AuthProvider` |\n< | `faucet-source-rest` | `crates/source/rest/` | REST API source — auth, pagination, extraction, schema inference |\n< | `faucet-source-graphql` | `crates/source/graphql/` | GraphQL API source — cursor pagination, variable injection |\n< | `faucet-source-xml` | `crates/source/xml/` | XML/SOAP API source — XML-to-JSON conversion, dot-path extraction |\n< | `faucet-source-grpc` | `crates/source/grpc/` | gRPC source — dynamic protobuf via `prost-reflect`; unary and server-streaming RPCs |\n< | `faucet-source-postgres` | `crates/source/postgres/` | PostgreSQL query source — run SQL, return rows as JSON |\n< | `faucet-source-postgres-cdc` | `crates/source/postgres-cdc/` | PostgreSQL CDC (logical replication) source — pgoutput decoder, slot lifecycle, resumable via state store |\n< | `faucet-source-mysql` | `crates/source/mysql/` | MySQL query source |\n< | `faucet-source-mysql-cdc` | `crates/source/mysql-cdc/` | MySQL CDC source — binlog row events, file/pos or GTID bookmarks |\n< | `faucet-source-mssql-cdc` | `crates/source/mssql-cdc/` | Microsoft SQL Server CDC source — change-tracking/CDC tables, LSN bookmarks |\n< | `faucet-source-mssql` | `crates/source/mssql/` | Microsoft SQL Server query source (tiberius) |\n< | `faucet-source-sqlite` | `crates/source/sqlite/` | SQLite query source |\n< | `faucet-source-duckdb` | `crates/source/duckdb/` | DuckDB query source — file or `:memory:`; blocking-task + channel streaming, rows as JSON |\n< | `faucet-source-sqs` | `crates/source/sqs/` | AWS SQS source — long-poll ReceiveMessage, delete-after-emit (at-least-once), idle/max termination |\n< | `faucet-source-nats` | `crates/source/nats/` | NATS source — subject subscription or JetStream durable consumer, idle/max termination |\n< | `faucet-source-sftp` | `crates/source/sftp/` | SFTP source — list/glob a remote dir over SSH; JSONL, JSON array, raw text |\n< | `faucet-source-s3` | `crates/source/s3/` | AWS S3 source — JSONL, JSON array, or raw text |\n< | `faucet-source-gcs` | `crates/source/gcs/` | Google Cloud Storage source — JSONL, JSON array, or raw text |\n< | `faucet-source-mongodb` | `crates/source/mongodb/` | MongoDB source — find() with filter/projection/sort |\n< | `faucet-source-mongodb-cdc` | `crates/source/mongodb-cdc/` | MongoDB CDC source — Change Streams, resumeToken bookmarks |\n< | `faucet-source-redis` | `crates/source/redis/` | Redis source — streams, lists, key patterns |\n< | `faucet-source-webhook` | `crates/source/webhook/` | Webhook source — temporary HTTP server collecting POSTs |\n< | `faucet-source-websocket` | `crates/source/websocket/` | WebSocket source — live streaming, subscription frames, reconnect |\n< | `faucet-source-csv` | `crates/source/csv/` | CSV file source |\n< | `faucet-source-elasticsearch` | `crates/source/elasticsearch/` | Elasticsearch source — search/scroll API |\n< | `faucet-source-parquet` | `crates/source/parquet/` | Parquet source — local, glob, or S3; vectorized Arrow async reader, projection |\n< | `faucet-source-delta` | `crates/source/delta/` | Delta Lake source — local FS or S3/Azure/GCS; time travel, projection pushdown, partition reconstruction |\n< | `faucet-source-kafka` | `crates/source/kafka/` | Kafka consumer — subscribes to topics, drains with idle/max-messages termination |\n< | `faucet-source-kinesis` | `crates/source/kinesis/` | AWS Kinesis source — per-shard GetRecords workers, sequence-number bookmarks |\n< | `faucet-source-bigquery` | `crates/source/bigquery/` | BigQuery query source — `jobs.query` + `jobs.getQueryResults`, pageToken pagination, type-aware row decoding |\n< | `faucet-source-snowflake` | `crates/source/snowflake/` | Snowflake query source — SQL REST API with server-side partition pagination, JWT / OAuth auth |\n< | `faucet-source-databricks` | `crates/source/databricks/` | Databricks SQL source — Statement Execution API; async poll, chunk pagination, typed decode, incremental bookmark |\n< | `faucet-source-spanner` | `crates/source/spanner/` | Cloud Spanner source — streaming SQL (gRPC), incremental replication, stale reads, PK-range sharding |\n< | `faucet-source-redshift` | `crates/source/redshift/` | Amazon Redshift query source — run SQL, typed row decode, connection pool |\n< | `faucet-source-clickhouse` | `crates/source/clickhouse/` | ClickHouse query source — HTTP protocol, rows as JSON |\n< | `faucet-source-pubsub` | `crates/source/pubsub/` | Google Cloud Pub/Sub source — streaming pull, ack at durable page boundaries, resumable termination |\n< | `faucet-source-azure-blob` | `crates/source/azure-blob/` | Azure Blob Storage / ADLS Gen2 source — JSONL, JSON array, or raw text |\n< | `faucet-source-singer` | `crates/source/singer/` | Singer bridge source — runs an external Singer tap; NDJSON over stdout, STATE→bookmark (Tier-2 / experimental) |\n< | `faucet-sink-bigquery` | `crates/sink/bigquery/` | BigQuery sink — `tabledata.insertAll` streaming; in-place `MERGE` for upsert + effectively-once |\n< | `faucet-sink-postgres` | `crates/sink/postgres/` | PostgreSQL sink — multi-row `INSERT` (JSONB or mapped cols); `COPY FROM STDIN` fast-path |\n< | `faucet-sink-jsonl` | `crates/sink/jsonl/` | JSON Lines file sink |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"28ae507f-5383-413d-b6e9-840abaa59698","timestamp":"2026-08-24T09:17:53.435Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== replicate clone exists? ===\n-rw-r--r--  1 c-sikawats  staff  85452  1 Aug 07:11 /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/replicate/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md\n=== is the replicate CLAUDE.md a symlink already? ===\n(regular file, not a symlink)\n\n=== sizes / line counts ===\n     213 /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md\n     596 /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/replicate/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md\n     809 total\n\n=== diff (replicate vs current) — lines only in replicate (<) could be valuable ===\n3c3\n< ## Library Purpose\n---\n> `faucet-stream` is a modular, config-driven Rust data-pipeline toolkit: pluggable **source** and **sink** connectors plus a `faucet` CLI binary that runs pipelines declaratively from YAML/JSON (no Rust code required). Cargo workspace, 92 crates (91 libraries + the `faucet-cli` binary); all connector crates depend only on `faucet-core`, and the umbrella `faucet-stream` + the CLI pull in every connector via optional features. `faucet serve` (opt-in) adds a long-running HTTP control-plane runtime alongside one-shot `run` and the `schedule` cron runtime.\n5c5\n< `faucet-stream` is a modular, config-driven data pipeline toolkit for Rust with pluggable **source** and **sink** connectors, plus a `faucet` CLI binary that runs pipelines declaratively from YAML/JSON — no Rust code required.\n---\n> This file holds the **always-on rules**. Situational detail lives in on-demand reference files under `.claude/rules/` (see below) — read the relevant one when its trigger applies.\n7,9c7\n< - **Sources** fetch data from external systems (e.g. REST APIs).\n< - **Sinks** write data to external systems (e.g. BigQuery).\n< - **`faucet` CLI** (`cli/`) wires source → trans