{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","prNumber":577,"prUrl":"https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/577","prRepository":"faucet-hq/faucet-stream","timestamp":"2026-08-24T09:41:43.497Z"}
{"parentUuid":"8b15ffe3-b159-4a34-a19b-93c424ec79b4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeMMWKGxd8Bk9a6k6seVd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7469,"cache_read_input_tokens":928100,"output_tokens":7448,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6091},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7448,"cache_read_input_tokens":928100,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7469},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeMMWEGq1d5k8eMfXRLtb","type":"assistant","uuid":"f57e75ce-f0c8-4010-bfa0-83b98e065873","timestamp":"2026-08-24T09:43:11.874Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/sinks-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"f57e75ce-f0c8-4010-bfa0-83b98e065873","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeMMWKGxd8Bk9a6k6seVd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I can see exactly why this happens. It's not release-plz being dumb — it's how the internal versions are **pinned**.\n\n## Diagnosis\n\nIn the root `Cargo.toml`:\n```toml\n[workspace.dependencies]\nfaucet-core = { path = \"crates/core\", version = \"1.11.0\" }   # ← exact minor, and\n```\nand every dependent uses `faucet-core.workspace = true`.\n\nSo when `faucet-core` bumps 1.10.0 → 1.11.0, release-plz **rewrites** that `version = \"1.10.0\"` → `\"1.11.0\"` (its default: tighten each internal dep to the version just released). Because ~50 crates inherit it via `.workspace = true`, that single line-edit changes every dependent's effective manifest → release-plz republishes each with a patch bump and the \"Updated the following local packages: faucet-core\" note. `faucet-sink-mysql 1.7.1` is exactly that — no real change, just the pin moving.\n\nThe trigger is the **exact-minor pin + release-plz auto-tightening**, not any real code change.\n\n## Structural fix — loosen internal reqs to major-only\n\nChange the internal deps from an exact minor to a caret-major:\n```toml\n[workspace.dependencies]\nfaucet-core            = { path = \"crates/core\", version = \"1\" }\nfaucet-auth            = { path = \"crates/auth\", version = \"1\" }\nfaucet-common-bigquery = { path = \"crates/common/bigquery\", version = \"1\" }\n# … all the internal faucet-* crates\n```\nNow a `faucet-core` 1.10 → 1.11 bump **already satisfies `\"1\"`**, so release-plz has nothing to rewrite → it leaves each dependent's manifest untouched → **dependents bump only when they have their own `feat`/`fix`/`perf` commits.** The cascade disappears.\n\n**Why this is safe here specifically** — it rests on an invariant you already enforce:\n- `faucet-core` has a **required `cargo-semver-checks` CI gate**, so its 1.x public API is guaranteed backward-compatible. Any 1.x `faucet-core` is API-compatible with any dependent built against 1.x — which is the whole premise `\"1\"` relies on.\n- Every crate is `1.0.0+` (your hard rule), so caret-major is meaningful.\n- Cargo resolves **newest-compatible by default**, so a real user of `faucet-sink-mysql` still gets the latest `faucet-core 1.x`.\n\n**Honest tradeoff:** the published dep requirement becomes looser (`faucet-core >=1,<2`). The only failure mode is a downstream build forcing **`-Z minimal-versions`**, which could pick an older `faucet-core` missing a newer API a sink uses — a theoretical concern the default resolver never hits, and irrelevant to the umbrella `faucet-stream` / `faucet-cli` users (those keep exact pins and are what most people consume). If you'd rather keep a floor, `\"1.x\"` (major.minor) is a middle ground — but note it re-introduces the cascade on **minor** bumps, so major-only is the true decoupler.\n\n## Alternatives (weaker)\n- **Accept it** — patch bumps are cheap and the changelog says \"dependency update,\" so it's not *wrong*, just noisy. Many workspaces live with it for the tightness guarantee.\n- There's no release-plz toggle that says \"don't bump dependents but keep exact pins\" — the pin style *is* the lever, which is why the `\"1\"` change is the structural answer.\n\nMy recommendation: go major-only (`\"1\"`) for the internal `faucet-*` deps. It's a one-time root-`Cargo.toml` edit, and I'd validate it with a release-plz dry-run (`release-plz release-pr` locally) to confirm the cascade is gone before trusting it on the next real release.\n\nWant me to make the change (loosen all internal `faucet-*` workspace deps to `\"1\"`) and dry-run it? I'd do it as its own small PR so you can see the effect in isolation."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7469,"cache_read_input_tokens":928100,"output_tokens":7448,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6091},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7469,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7448,"cache_read_input_tokens":928100,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7469},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeMMWEGq1d5k8eMfXRLtb","type":"assistant","uuid":"09d6acf3-3398-44ff-9725-7b78ed4e13fc","timestamp":"2026-08-24T09:43:29.106Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/sinks-auto-create-table","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
